<%# THE DEFECT, REPRODUCED ON PURPOSE — the control for the leak regression.
    This is the shape the picker shipped with once: a slot taken as a BLOCK and
    guarded with block_given?. Inside a compiled Rails partial block_given? is
    ALWAYS true, because PartialRenderer hands the template a block either way,
    so with no caller block the yield falls through to view_flow and prints the
    entire captured page body inside the card.

    It exists so the regression test can prove its probe still BITES. Asserting
    only that the shipped card is clean is satisfied by a harness that renders
    nothing, populates no flow, or looks in the wrong element — every one of
    which passes forever while the guard is dead. This card makes the harness
    demonstrate a leak it can actually see. %>
<div class="leaky-root"><% if block_given? %><%= yield %><% end %></div>
